# Private zoend for invite lookup. Omit locally to fail-open the stub.
# ZOEN_IDENTITY_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:58701

# Google + Apple are AuthKit dashboard toggles, not process env.
# This package never reads GOOGLE_* or APPLE_* secrets. Do not add a second OAuth stack.
#
# Staging (WorkOS default credentials, no custom OAuth apps):
#   Dashboard → Authentication → OAuth providers
#   Google + Apple: Enabled with WorkOS demo credentials.
#   Redirects: https://zoen.tironi.xyz/auth/workos/callback
#              http://localhost:3000/auth/workos/callback
# Email + password stays on; AuthKit enables it by default.
#
# WhatsApp mint is always https://zoen.tironi.xyz/onboard/{token}
# Never app.zoen.local. This package serves that page. zoend keeps its route until callers migrate.
#
# CLI Auth (zoen login on laptop/VFS/herdr) is a different grant on the same WorkOS app.
# Agent polls. Person still does Google/Apple on hosted AuthKit.
# Do not print a bare device/user code in WhatsApp.
